1
00:00:00,343 --> 00:00:05,452
Management · people and teams — Keep the people records, the teams, and who works on what — with how many hours.

2
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:10,773
Management holds WorkDesk's records. Each button along the top opens one list.

3
00:00:11,584 --> 00:00:16,687
People: everyone in the company, with their email and mobile — click either to copy it.

4
00:00:17,508 --> 00:00:24,887
The role decides what a person may do. Open the list and pick a new role — the mouse wheel never changes it by accident.

5
00:00:25,896 --> 00:00:31,273
Portal access decides which apps they see on the Employee Portal home page. The pencil changes it.

6
00:00:34,306 --> 00:00:39,386
WorkDesk on or off, a Taskana role, the Handbook and the Knowledge Base — one person at a time.

7
00:00:42,052 --> 00:00:49,114
The pencil by the name edits a person's details: job title, team, manager, contract hours, birthday… Deactivate closes an account without deleting its history.

8
00:00:52,972 --> 00:00:57,580
Teams group people under a lead. Each card shows the team's clients and members.

9
00:00:58,244 --> 00:01:04,256
People without a team wait under Available people. Placing someone in a team makes its lead their direct manager.

10
00:01:06,514 --> 00:01:13,044
Manage opens a team to change its members and lead. Request a team member borrows someone from another team — that goes to approval.

11
00:01:16,232 --> 00:01:22,238
Assignments &amp; Allowances: who may report Yellow hours on which project or work order — and how many hours they get.

12
00:01:29,784 --> 00:01:35,143
Done. Time beyond the allowance still gets reported — it just goes to a manager's approval first.

13
00:01:35,784 --> 00:01:42,384
Pending Activation lists new accounts waiting to be approved, and the Verification Queue checks clients and projects people typed in themselves.

14
00:01:43,086 --> 00:01:47,712
People · teams · assignments — Next: clients, projects, work orders and budgets. More help: the Handbook → Management.
